      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-344005",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$8x^{2}y^{\u2033} + 2x(4x + 1)y^{\u2032} + y = 0$\nWhich of the following is a Frobenius series solution to the differential equation given above, where $a_{n}$ for $n = 0, 1, 2, \u2026$ are constants determined by substitution?\n\n*Hint: Substituting a trial Frobenius series solution into each term of the ODE, we obtain*\n$8x^{2}y^{\u2033}|= 8(\u03bb^{2} - \u03bb)a_{0}x^{\u03bb} + 8\u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)((\u03bb + n)^{2} - (\u03bb + n))a_{n}x^{\u03bb + n},; 2x(4x + 1)y^{\u2032}|= 2\u03bba_{0}x^{\u03bb} + \u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)[8(\u03bb + m - 1)a_{n - 1} + 2(\u03bb + n)a_{n}]x^{\u03bb + n},; y|= a_{0}x^{\u03bb} + x^{\u03bb}\u2211_(n = 1)^(\u221e)a_{n}x^{\u03bb + n}$."
