      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-345279",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n9{x}^{2}{y}^{\u2033}+12x{y}^{\u2032}+(9x-2)y=0\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is a Frobenius series solution to the differential equation, where ${a}_{n}$ for $n=0,1,2,\u2026$ are constants determined by substitution?\n\n*Hint: Substituting a trial Frobenius series solution into each term of the ODE, we obtain*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}{y}^{\u2033} & =9({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }9((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ 12x{y}^{\u2032} & =12\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }12(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ (9x-2)y & =-2{a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(9{a}_{n-1}-2{a}_{n}){x}^{\\lambda +n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
