      ":question/problem": "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}{y}^{\u2033}+x(6x-1){y}^{\u2032}-3y=0\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is a Frobenius series solution to the differential equation given above, where ${a}_{n}$ for $n=0,1,2,\u2026$ are constants determined by substitution?\n\n*Hint: Substituting a trial Frobenius series solution into each term of the ODE, we obtain*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}{y}^{\u2033} & =6({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+6{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ x(6x-1){y}^{\u2032} & =-\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }[6(\\lambda +n-1){a}_{n-1}-(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}]{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ -3y & =-3{a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }-3{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
